const ARCHIVE={"2026":{"live":true},"2025":{"races":24,"champ":["Lando Norris","McLaren",423],"p2":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",421],"p3":["Oscar Piastri","McLaren",410],"cons":["McLaren",833],"wins":"7 wins for Norris","sum":"McLaren had the fastest car for most of the year and Oscar Piastri led the standings through the summer. Verstappen mounted a late charge in a slower Red Bull, turning it into a three-way fight that went to Abu Dhabi, where Norris took his first title by two points.","keys":["McLaren clinched the constructors' title with six rounds to spare.","Hamilton's first season at Ferrari ended without a Grand Prix win.","Final year of the 2022–2025 ground-effect rules."]},"2024":{"races":24,"champ":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",437],"p2":["Lando Norris","McLaren",374],"p3":["Charles Leclerc","Ferrari",356],"cons":["McLaren",666],"wins":"9 wins for Verstappen","sum":"Verstappen won seven of the first ten races, then Red Bull lost its edge as McLaren upgraded its car. Norris took his first win in Miami, but Verstappen's consistency and a drive from 17th to win in wet Brazil secured a fourth straight title.","keys":["McLaren won its first constructors' title since 1998.","A record 24-race calendar.","Seven different drivers won races."]},"2023":{"races":22,"champ":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",575],"p2":["Sergio Pérez","Red Bull Racing",285],"p3":["Lewis Hamilton","Mercedes",234],"cons":["Red Bull Racing",860],"wins":"19 wins for Verstappen","sum":"The most dominant season in F1 history. Red Bull won 21 of 22 Grands Prix, with Carlos Sainz's Singapore victory the only exception, and Verstappen set records for wins in a season and consecutive wins.","keys":["Verstappen won 10 races in a row.","Las Vegas returned to the calendar on the Strip.","Sprint format expanded to six weekends."]},"2022":{"races":22,"champ":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",454],"p2":["Charles Leclerc","Ferrari",308],"p3":["Sergio Pérez","Red Bull Racing",305],"cons":["Red Bull Racing",759],"wins":"15 wins for Verstappen","sum":"Ground-effect rules arrived and Ferrari started strongest, with Leclerc winning two of the first three races. Reliability failures and strategy errors let Red Bull take over, and Verstappen clinched his second title in Japan.","keys":["First year of the ground-effect regulations.","Miami joined the calendar.","Mercedes won only one race, in Brazil."]},"2021":{"races":22,"champ":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",395.5],"p2":["Lewis Hamilton","Mercedes",387.5],"p3":["Valtteri Bottas","Mercedes",226],"cons":["Mercedes",613.5],"wins":"10 wins for Verstappen","sum":"Verstappen and Hamilton fought all year, with collisions at Silverstone and Monza. They arrived in Abu Dhabi level on points, and a disputed safety car restart on the final lap gave Verstappen his first title.","keys":["Mercedes won an eighth straight constructors' title.","Sprint qualifying debuted at Silverstone.","Race director Michael Masi was replaced after the finale."]},"2020":{"races":17,"champ":["Lewis Hamilton","Mercedes",347],"p2":["Valtteri Bottas","Mercedes",223],"p3":["Max Verstappen","Red Bull Racing",214],"cons":["Mercedes",573],"wins":"11 wins for Hamilton","sum":"The pandemic delayed the start until July in Austria, with a reshaped 17-race calendar that brought back Imola, Portimão, Mugello and the Nürburgring. Hamilton won his seventh title, equalling Michael Schumacher's record.","keys":["Pierre Gasly won at Monza for AlphaTauri.","Sergio Pérez took his first win in Sakhir.","Romain Grosjean escaped a fiery crash in Bahrain."]}};
